sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Client
  participant A as API
  participant P as Participation Service
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant O as Outbox
  participant W as Workers

  Note over C,A: Admission/ticket action is independent.\nExternal ticket purchase does not confirm Meet participation.

  C->>A: POST /occurrences/{id}/join + Idempotency-Key
  A->>P: authorize + revalidate occurrence + ParticipationMode
  P->>DB: transaction / capacity lock or constraint-safe reserve
  DB-->>P: current occurrence state + existing participation
  alt OPEN + capacity
    P->>DB: CONFIRMED participation
  else APPROVAL_REQUIRED
    P->>DB: REQUESTED participation
  else full + waitlist enabled
    P->>DB: WAITLISTED entry
  else INVITE_ONLY without invite / DISABLED / cancelled
    P-->>A: deterministic domain error
  end
  P->>O: insert domain event in same transaction
  P-->>A: stable logical outcome
  A-->>C: authoritative response
  O->>W: publish after commit
  W-->>C: push/realtime hint
  Note over C,A: Client treats API/REST state as truth;\npush/realtime may be missed or duplicated.
